  "label": "Hostility mapped onto Queen Elizabeth II",
  "description": "The text 'kill them' is superimposed over the image of Queen Elizabeth II, creating an analogical mapping where the violent command is projected onto her as the target. This mapping is abusive, as it associates the revered monarch with extreme violence, using her visual presence to embody the hostile sentiment expressed in the text. The mapping is reinforced by the juxtaposition of her dignified appearance with the aggressive text, creating a jarring contrast that intensifies the meme's provocative intent.",
